{"h": {"measure": "P", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 122, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding the input-to-output residual where none existed gives a large gain, whereas replacing a conv or pool on edge 3 with skip changes little."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Turning a missing node2->output edge into a 3x3 conv adds a whole computational path, a much larger gain than swapping an existing op."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty node1->output edge with a 3x3 conv adds capacity and a new path, beating replacement of pool, skip or 1x1."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 0 is none, node 1 is dead, so a conv there revives edges 2 and 4 and yields a larger improvement."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv where there was no input->node2 edge adds a parallel path, worth more than replacing pool or skip."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "If edge 4 is none, node 1 feeds the output only through edge 2, so removing edge 0 costs less than when node 1 connects directly to the output."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 2 absent, removing edge 1 leaves node 2 with no input and kills the edge-5 path, so the loss is much larger."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 5 is none, edge 4 is the only conv path to the output, so removing it collapses the cell to a near-identity and hurts much more."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 4 is none, removing the edge-3 skip can leave the output with few or no live inputs, which is far more damaging."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Without the input->output skip, a skip on edge 4 adds a near-residual shortcut that helps gradient flow, so it is worth more than when edge 3 already provides one."}], "tok": 30607, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3"], [4, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3"], [4, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [4, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [4, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["none", "none", "non